{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinGradeConnective","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinGradeConnective","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationBridge","lean:module:QOU.Information.SurrealBudgetGrade"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_polyObservable_family_of_horizon_cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_polyObservable_family_of_horizon_cost","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinGradeConnective.lean#L68-L85","doc":"**Every polynomial budget fails on a horizon-cost family (sorry-free).**\nUpgrades `SkeinObservationSystem.not_polyObservable_id_of_horizon_cost` from\nthe identity budget to *any* `PolyBounded` budget.  For a size-indexed family\n`P n` with filtration level `n`, whose observation is reached only at the\nhorizon cost `3^n` (`hcost`), no polynomial budget `poly` is\n`PolyObservable` for all `n` — because `3^n` is super-polynomial\n(`superPoly_three_pow`), so it eventually exceeds `poly`.  This is the\nsurreal ω-grade squeeze applied to the Skein bridge's P-vs-NP leg.  It is the\n`cost = 3^n` instance of `not_polyObservable_family_of_superPoly` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_polyObservable_family_of_superPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_polyObservable_family_of_superPoly","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinGradeConnective.lean#L44-L66","doc":"**The general super-poly-cost separation (sorry-free).**  For any\n`SkeinObservationSystem`, a size-indexed family `P n` at filtration level `n`\nwhose observation is reached only at a **super-polynomial** cost `cost n`\n(`hcost`, `hcost_sp`) is not `PolyObservable` for all `n` under any polynomial\nbudget — `cost` eventually exceeds every polynomial.  The horizon\n(`cost = 3^n`) and moduli (`cost = physicalCost = 3^{3n}`,\n`PNeqNpWallUnification`) separations are its two instances. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.horizon_cost_not_polyBounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.horizon_cost_not_polyBounded","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinGradeConnective.lean#L38-L42","doc":"**The horizon cost `3^n` is not polynomially budgeted (sorry-free).**  The\ngrade form of the bridge's P-vs-NP separation: the `3^c` resolution-tree cost\nout-grades every polynomial budget. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.superPoly_three_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.superPoly_three_pow","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinGradeConnective.lean#L32-L36","doc":"**`3^n` is super-polynomial (sorry-free).**  `2^n ≤ 3^n` lifts\n`superPoly_two_pow` through `SuperPolynomial.of_le`; the resolution-tree\nhorizon cost lives in the super-poly grade. ","signatureChunk":0}]}